# The programs of this corpus that paint a page and never ask for it.
# One basename per line.
#
# An encapsulated file is a figure for another document to place, and
# the document supplies the showpage: a file of that shape carries none
# of its own, so the only page it produces is the one the interpreter
# ends for a job that painted and stopped. That is the whole of what
# these four put on paper, and it is why they are in the corpus -- the
# rest of it would render the same whether that page were ended or
# thrown away.
#
# Read off the files rather than off a run: the entry says the program
# carries no showpage, which is a fact about the text, and the text is
# where it is checked. Every program of the corpus is scanned with its
# comment tails removed and held to this register both ways, so a name
# here whose program does ask for its page fails, and a program that
# stops asking without being named here fails too -- either is the
# corpus quietly ceasing to cover the behaviour while still reporting
# twelve programs rendered. An empty register fails for the same
# reason.
#
# All four are ImageMagick's encapsulated wrapper around a photograph:
# one image operator, no showpage, and nothing else on the page.
football_logo
icam_logo
sc_logo
scs_logo
